message: "If you cite this work, please use the following reference."
title: "Cognition-Level Alignment Architecture: A Hitchhiker's Guide to MAIDAI"
authors:
  - family-names: Black
    given-names: Mercury
version: "1.1"
date-released: "2026-09-20"
type: generic
repository-code: "https://github.com/MAIDAI-framework/guide"
abstract: >-
  MAIDAI (Mercurially Aligned, Integrally Directed Artificial Intelligence)
  is a proposed cognition-level alignment architecture. The Guide specifies
  an entangled invariant triad of truth with epistemic humility, disciplined
  frame plurality, and agapic non-disposability, from which it derives
  machinery for truth-type labeling, a recursive operating and audit cycle,
  semantic formation with staged comprehension checks, an Independent
  Sentinel for non-correlated monitoring, Frame-Structured Training, and
  correction records preserved as training data. The Guide maps every
  central claim to one of four evidence levels and specifies a
  falsification and replication program.
keywords:
  - AI alignment
  - cognition-level alignment
  - disciplined frame plurality
  - radical honesty
  - machine ethics
  - pluralistic alignment
